cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this package in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
title: "SF Multicell Twin: An Open 5G NR Ray-Tracing Lab (Sionna RT on a Free T4)"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-13
authors:
  - family-names: Yenamandra
    given-names: Rao S.
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ysrao/twin5GNR-multicell-SF"
url: "https://ysrao.github.io/twin5GNR-multicell-SF/twin5GNR-multicell-SionnaRT-EvalMesh-Nov13.html"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible 5G NR multicell ray-tracing package: a three-site,
  nine-sector layout at 3.6 GHz traced with Sionna RT over a downtown
  San Francisco city tile, runnable end-to-end on a free Colab T4 with
  reader-local data, with CSV-driven tower-shift experiments and an
  interactive artefact wired to the trace output. Includes a controlled
  comparison showing that city-mesh provenance is a first-order variable
  in ray-traced coverage.
keywords:
  - 5G NR
  - ray tracing
  - Sionna RT
  - digital twin
  - radio propagation
  - open educational resource
